## Scope

Publishes the reviewed, UI-independent Python reference continuation for issue #4271 on exact corrected #4270 parent `920c46dee688815691e251777142126bf1489b1a`.

This is a bounded first slice, not issue closure: it qualifies one immutable arbitrary-orientation plane with an optional finite tangent-axis edge. Changing normals, material regions, terrain deformation, UI, compiled runtimes, and downstream parity remain explicitly open.

## Delivered

- kinetic Coulomb skid, static-feasibility gate, pure roll, rolling resistance, retained axial spin, qualified rest, and exact finite-edge termination;
- adaptive oblique-slip integration preventing zero-manifold overshoot and step-size resonance while preserving exact collinear capture;
- passive translation/rotation/gravity/moving-surface work ledger and distinct skid/roll paths;
- canonical request SHA-256 binding across impact, bounce, skid/roll, and composition phases;
- strict terminal state/trajectory/event/termination consistency and fail-closed unrepresentable outcomes;
- composed two-phase model identity, enduring impact material limitations, and removal of fulfilled stage-only notices;
- exact prefix/suffix composition without duplicate or fabricated epsilon timestamps;
- scientific specification, campaign manifest, SPEC update, and all three canonical handoffs.

## Independent review corrections

The initial local implementation was withheld after review found six blockers. The reviewed implementation lineage includes regressions and fixes for oblique-slope convergence, zero-speed downhill starts, immediate outward edge departure, cross-request prefix reuse, contradictory final-state evidence, and stale #4302 carrier metadata. The reviewer re-ran the adversarial sweep and confirmed every blocker closed before publication.

Hosted quality-gate run `31354071845` then exposed ten deterministic MyPy 1.13 `no-any-return` findings because the changed-file CI lane uses `--follow-imports=skip`. Immutable corrected implementation `f475ae85feea1b2c628f756699b2aba6ea9334fb` explicitly normalizes the already validated NumPy-backed scalar boundaries to `float`/`bool`; physics, values, integration ordering, schema, output, API, scope, and base are unchanged.

## Verification

- 115/115 full ground tests on CPython 3.11.9;
- 115/115 on isolated real CPython 3.10.20 (five expected missing-plugin configuration warnings only);
- exact hosted-style and full-package pinned MyPy 1.13 clean across all 25 ground production modules;
- pinned Ruff 0.14.10 check/format clean for the corrected production files and previously clean full package;
- campaign manifest validator plus 8/8 manifest contract tests;
- documentation governance, changed-test assertion, structural, file-size, and diff gates.

## Exact stack state

- Base branch: `feat/4270-ground-impact-bounce`
- Exact parent: `920c46dee688815691e251777142126bf1489b1a`
- Immutable corrected implementation evidence: `f475ae85feea1b2c628f756699b2aba6ea9334fb`
- Current documentation/evidence carrier: `482cdf272b04c78b50da91a6d2ddd4d15e063c7b`
- No retarget, rebase, force-push, parent rewrite, admin merge, or protected-check bypass was used.

Issue #4271 remains open until regional/changing-normal surfaces and its remaining acceptance criteria are implemented and protected release evidence exists. Fresh protected CI and review remain required; the failed hosted run was not manually retried.
